# CODEOWNERS for clawmind
#
# GitHub uses this file to require review from the listed owners before a
# pull request can be merged into a protected branch. We keep ownership
# coarse on purpose: a single maintainer reviewing every change is the
# correct model for a project of this size, and procurement teams running
# SOC2 readiness checks expect to see a CODEOWNERS file under .github/.
#
# Format reference: https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-security/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Order matters: the last matching pattern wins, so the catch-all stays at
# the top and more specific rules layer on below.

